    "size": 1712,
    "content": "========================================================================\n     NGUYEN'S AI — GEMINI EDITION (WINDOWS AUTOMATION)\n========================================================================\n\n1. QUICK START (TWO WAYS TO RUN):\n\n   METHOD 1: COMMAND PROMPT / CLI (RECOMMENDED & FASTEST)\n   - Double-click 'run.bat' (or 'cli.bat').\n   - Paste your Google Gemini API Key when prompted.\n     (Keys are stored encrypted locally on your Windows PC via DPAPI).\n   - Type your task (e.g., \"open notepad\", \"open chrome and search news\").\n   - (Optional) Provide a reference image path if you want Gemini to inspect a screenshot or picture.\n   - Press ENTER -> The mouse moves to targets and executes the task!\n\n   METHOD 2: WEB CONTROL PANEL\n   - Double-click 'web.bat'.\n   - Your browser will open at: http://127.0.0.1:8765/\n   - Enter your prompt, attach optional reference images, and click \"Review & Run\".\n\n2. EMERGENCY STOP:\n   - Press [Ctrl + Fn + E] (or Ctrl + E) at ANY time for instant cut-off.\n   - OR move your mouse to the top-left corner of your screen (0, 0).\n   - OR double-click 'stop.bat'.\n   - OR press Ctrl + C in the Command Prompt window.\n\n3. FILES INCLUDED:\n   - run.bat / cli.bat : Instant Command Prompt launchers\n   - web.bat           : Web GUI launcher\n   - stop.bat          : Instant kill switch\n   - NguyeensCLI.ps1   : Interactive console script\n   - NguyeensAI.ps1    : Local web server and API handler\n   - worker.ps1        : Gemini Vision loop & mouse/keyboard automation\n   - web/index.html    : Local web GUI\n   - data/settings.json: Settings configuration\n   - data/memory.json  : Persistent memory rules storage (reinforces output)\n   - README.md         : Documentation\n",
    "language": "text",
    "description": "Plain text quick start and emergency stop guide"
